Rule 6 (input tensor must have positive shape dimensions when non-scalar)
{v_1: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 7 (both tensors must have consistent dimensionality and matching first dimension)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0))
>>
Rule 8 (tensors with same shape must have equal total elements)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≠ ndim(v_2) ∨ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 15 (both tensors must have matching first dimension size if non-scalar)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 0 ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 16 (input and other tensors must have equal last dimension if multi-dimensional)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) < 2 ∨ ndim(v_2) < 2 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1)
>>
Rule 17 (tensors with same dimensionality must have matching middle dimensions)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≠ ndim(v_2) ∨ ndim(v_1) ≤ 1 ∨ ∀i ∈ [1, ndim(v_1) - 2]: shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 18 (both tensors must be non-empty for valid comparison)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) > 0 ∧ ∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1]: shape(v_2, j) > 0
